From 22c3c5b5238a2420c37d134d82ba9ddad922d354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kk <kaiwalya.khasnis57@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 10:22:23 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] SystemUI: add a flashlight strength dialog

Long press on the flashlight tile now opens a "Flashlight Strength"
dialog modelled on the one in Android 16: a vertical slider drawn as a
light beam above a flashlight icon, a Turn on/off button and Done.

The strength is written to a system property that the camera HAL reads,
named by config_flashlightStrengthProperty, with one value per level in
config_flashlightStrengthValues. Both are empty by default, which keeps
the old long press behaviour. While the torch is on, changes are applied
right away by turning the torch on again; only the latest level is sent
while dragging.

Settings can open the same dialog with the protected broadcast
com.android.systemui.action.SHOW_FLASHLIGHT_STRENGTH.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
